I'm not a statistician, but I do work in gerontology.  Survivorship
functions are properties of populations, cohorts, not individuals.
Estimating a survival curve for each individual doesn't make sense to me.
Is each individual in a different treatment group and you need the
survivorship function of each treatment group?

