I suspect that somewhere in the Splus filesystem there are some 
scripts that control some of these things. If someone would poke 
around, I'd bet we could have some good improvements. But not in the 
form of options. In the form of revising their scripts. 
Unfortunately, I've never felt I could justify the time it would 
take, relative to what my employer expects of me.

On my list are:

  - Help sub-windows open up with more lines

  - The ability to look at the help for more than one function at 
once. Kind of basic, huh?

  - Ability to print a help page

  - Better cross referencing, resulting in better searching

  - A complete set of help pages (some are missing)

  - Up to date help pages. For example, the current help page for 
module() omits one of the presumably new arguments.

AND up-to-date hardcopy help pages included with the distribution. As 
in a BOOK or MANUAL. I hate being restricted to online only.

I too have ended up using help() more than help.start(), especially 
since on the systems I have access to, Netscape grabs all the color 
resources, so I always have to remember to start my graphics device 
