Thanks very much to prof. B.D. Ripley.

Solution of my problem : I forgot an important thing : the names of the
.hlp, .cnt and .gid files must be same as the library name (in my case
nls2000 and not nls2 as it was).

The creation of compiled help files for S-PLUS 2000 from nroff help files is
well detailed in S programming but I remind it quickly :
let "castor" be the name of the library.
Create castor.rtf and castor.cnt files using prof. Ripley's nr2hlp perl
script (zip archive spwinhlp.zip available at
http://www.stats.ox.ac.uk/pub/SWin/).
Follow the instructions of the howto file that come with the archive to
create castor.hlp.
Put the files castor.hlp, castor.cnt and castor.gid in the castor directory
(which already contains _Data, _Prefs, and maybe funs and src directories).

